mips: an SDIO card can sit on the SD bus, and raise its interrupt

QEMU's SD bus assumes every card is an sdmmc-common (an SD or MMC
card).  Add an abstract TYPE_SD_BUS_CARD parent that sdmmc-common
derives from, so a device that is not an SD/MMC card -- an SDIO
function -- can sit on the bus by implementing SDCardClass itself.
sdbus_set_sdio_irq() lets such a card raise its interrupt to the host
controller, the way set_inserted/set_readonly already report upward.

Signed-off-by: OpenIPC <dev@openipc.org>

